<div class='header-badge'>BARION SYSTEM MASTER DOCUMENTATION • V2.0</div>
<h1>BARION SYSTEM MASTER GUIDE</h1>
<div class='tagline'>Learn Today. Heal Tomorrow.</div>

<div class='callout-info'>
  <strong>Document Purpose:</strong> Complete technical architecture, medical grounding rationale, competitive benchmarking matrix, onboarding manual, and ML Empowerment Build Challenge 3.0 hackathon submission playbook. Maintainable, verifiable, and structured for ongoing team collaboration.
</div>

<h2>1. Executive Summary & Vision</h2>
<p>
  <strong>Barion</strong> is an offline-first, source-grounded medical active-recall platform that transforms complex healthcare study materials (PDFs, clinical notes, pharmacological guidelines) into atomically precise study cards and interactive AI explanations with verbatim proof.
</p>
<p>
  Medical students face unprecedented cognitive load: preparing for the USMLE Step 1/Step 2, NCLEX, or board examinations requires retaining over 15,000 discrete medical facts across pharmacology, pathology, and clinical anatomy. Traditional tools fall short:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Generic LLMs (ChatGPT / Claude):</strong> Prone to lethal medical hallucinations—inventing plausible drug dosages, fabricating contraindications, or merging distinct mechanisms of action.</li>
  <li><strong>Traditional Flashcards (Anki / Quizlet):</strong> Require dozens of hours of manual flashcard creation or rely on outdated, unverified community decks without direct textbook citations.</li>
  <li><strong>Fragmented Workflows:</strong> Students juggle PDF readers, flashcard apps, search engines, and note-taking tools, wasting critical study hours on cognitive overhead.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Barion solves this with a mathematically grounded active-recall loop powered by the modern <strong>Free Spaced Repetition Scheduler (FSRS)</strong>, <strong>verbatim source-span verification</strong>, <strong>DailyMed/FDA authority checking</strong>, and <strong>Bari</strong>—a playful, expressive AI study companion.
</p>

