<h2>3. Core System Architecture</h2>
<p>
  Barion is built on a clean, decoupled, layered architecture:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Presentation Layer (React Native / Expo v57):</strong> Cross-platform mobile and web client built with TypeScript, Expo Router, and fluid Reanimated/Animated physics for Bari.</li>
  <li><strong>Domain & Repository Layer (src/storage/):</strong> Clean data access abstractions with transactional safety, query batching, and zero N+1 database patterns.</li>
  <li><strong>Storage Engine (medstudy.db via expo-sqlite):</strong> SQLite database with WAL (Write-Ahead Logging) journaling, strict foreign keys, compound indexes, and versioned schema migrations (Database Version 22).</li>
  <li><strong>AI Gateway (services/ai_gateway/):</strong> FastAPI Python service orchestrating Google Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite LLM calls, structured JSON schema enforcement, token budget capping, and rate-limiting.</li>
  <li><strong>Verification & Evaluation Service (services/card_evaluation/):</strong> Multi-agent verification coordinator cross-referencing candidates against FDA DailyMed labeling.</li>
</ol>

<h2>4. Spaced Repetition: FSRS Mathematical Model</h2>
<p>
  Barion implements the Free Spaced Repetition Scheduler (FSRS), modeling memory along three dimensions:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Difficulty (D in [1, 10]):</strong> How inherently difficult the clinical concept is to retrieve.</li>
  <li><strong>Stability (S > 0 days):</strong> The time in days required for retrievability to drop from 100% to 90%.</li>
  <li><strong>Retrievability (R in [0, 1]):</strong> The probability of successfully recalling the card at elapsed time t.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  When a student rates a card (<strong>Again</strong>, <strong>Hard</strong>, <strong>Good</strong>, <strong>Easy</strong>), FSRS updates stability and difficulty dynamically, scheduling intervals tailored to the individual learner.
</p>

<h2>5. Bari Mascot & Conversational Intelligence</h2>
<p>
  <strong>Bari</strong> is Barion's friendly blue mascot designed to reduce student exam anxiety and provide immediate, grounded explanations:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>3D Neu-morphic Design:</strong> Concentric depth glow rings, upper-left specular rim highlights, and ambient drop shadows.</li>
  <li><strong>Interactive Physics:</strong> Sinusoidal hovering float loop, breathing cycle, and elastic squash-and-stretch tap feedback.</li>
  <li><strong>Expression States:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><code>idle</code>: Gentle floating loop.</li>
      <li><code>thinking</code>: Subtle rocking oscillation with teal bulb badge.</li>
      <li><code>happy</code>: Celebratory pop with sparkle badge.</li>
      <li><code>explaining</code>: Attentive pulse with chat bubble badge.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Source-Strict RAG Chat:</strong> Bari uses only the imported document segments as evidence, rejecting off-source extrapolation to prevent misinformation.</li>
  <li><strong>Deterministic Fallback:</strong> If network or gateway is unavailable, Bari instantly falls back to local lexical retrieval.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. ML Empowerment Build Challenge 3.0 Hackathon Strategy</h2>
<p>
  Barion directly addresses all 5 official judging criteria:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Technical Implementation (30%):</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>FastAPI backend + React Native cross-platform app.</li>
      <li>Google Gemini integration with strict JSON schema compliance.</li>
      <li>Hybrid retrieval (BM25 + vector similarity + Reciprocal Rank Fusion).</li>
      <li>166 Python pytest tests + 189 Jest test suites passing.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Creativity & Innovation (20%):</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>First system combining verbatim source-span verification with FSRS spaced repetition.</li>
      <li>Interactive 3D Bari mascot transforming dry memorization into engaging active recall.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Real-World Impact (20%):</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Directly prevents medical study hallucinations for aspiring doctors and nurses.</li>
      <li>Democratizes USMLE/NCLEX board prep without expensive /year subscriptions.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Project Design & UX (15%):</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Minimalist medical aesthetic with dark hero card, progressive disclosure, and zero clutter.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Presentation & Documentation (15%):</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Complete documentation suite, structured benchmarks, and clear architecture blueprints.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<h2>7. Team Onboarding & Maintenance Playbook</h2>
<div class='callout'>
  <strong>Quickstart Command Checklist:</strong><br/>
  1. Install dependencies: <code>npm install</code><br/>
  2. Start AI Gateway: <code>python -m uvicorn services.ai_gateway.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8790</code><br/>
  3. Start Mobile/Web App: <code>npx expo start --web</code><br/>
  4. Run Type Check: <code>node node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit</code><br/>
  5. Run Jest Tests: <code>npm test -- --runInBand</code><br/>
  6. Run Python Tests: <code>python -m pytest services -p no:cacheprovider --basetemp=tmp/pytest_temp</code>
</div>

